 ## AGC 26.2 alpha10 - No-invasion scale remodel
 
 Alpha10 extends the no-invasion model from packet/chunk/world planning into large-server operation. `AGCPlayerIntentScheduler` gives each player deterministic FIFO tickets for cosmetic network work, chunk starts, entity tracker snapshots and arena bookkeeping. `AGCShardPlanner` assigns stable planning shards for multi-world and mini-game networks without changing Bukkit world ownership. `AGCPluginCompatibilityContracts` and the public `AGC.compatibility()` API let plugins declare conservative safety contracts instead of AGC guessing from plugin names. These contracts never permit off-thread Bukkit mutation or event-order changes; they only select read-only prepare, deadline batching, FIFO wait or ordered commit lanes.
+
+## AGC 26.2 alpha11 - aggressive performance standard
+
+Alpha11 remodels the optimisation stack around a hard shared performance standard instead of isolated per-feature heuristics.
+
+New runtime pieces:
+
+- `AGCPerformanceStandard` defines measurable SLOs: target MSPT, hard MSPT, one-tick packet deadline, ordered commit deadline, and semantic queue depth guard.
+- `AGCTickBudgetArbiter` centrally assigns per-tick budget units to network, chunk send/load/generate, entity snapshots, world prepare, player flow, mini-game prewarm and plugin commit lanes.
+- `AGCLatencySLO` records whether deadline batching and ordered commit drains stay inside their configured tick deadlines.
+- `AGCEntitySpatialSnapshotCache` caches read-only entity visibility summaries for the current tick only. It never owns live entity state and never skips entity ticks.
+- `AGCMinigameBurstPlanner` admits arena start/reset/prewarm bursts as read-only prepare or ordered commit work so many arenas can start without one arena stampeding the tick.
+
+The key rule remains strict: aggressive mode can spend more budget on read-only prepare and deadline batching, but it cannot drop packets, skip chunk queue heads, reorder per-player FIFO, mutate Bukkit state off-thread, or skip entity/gameplay ticks.
+
+New diagnostics:
+
+```text
+/agc hardperf
+```
+
+New plugin API helpers:
+
+- `AGC.performance().advise(AGCPerformanceIntent)`
+- `AGC.performance().denseArenaAdvice(players, entities, chunkRadius)`
+- `AGC.scheduler().readOnlySupplyAsync(...)`
+- `AGC.scheduler().prepareSupplyAsyncThenCommit(...)`
+- `AGC.minigames().performancePlan(...)`
