 - Added plugin compatibility contract API so minigame and infrastructure plugins can explicitly declare no-invasion-safe behaviours.
 - Added `/agc scale` and `/agc contracts` diagnostics.
 - Next: wire shard IDs into arena prewarm, player fanout snapshots and chunk IO admission metrics while keeping commit order unchanged.
+
+## Alpha11 gate - hard performance standard
+
+Alpha11 raises the implementation standard for every future optimisation:
+
+1. Every aggressive feature must request budget from `AGCTickBudgetArbiter` instead of privately delaying work.
+2. Every visible mutation must remain an ordered commit. Parallel work is limited to read-only prepare, snapshot planning, packet deadline batching and fair FIFO admission.
+3. Network batching must remain bounded by the configured one-tick SLO and must never drop packets.
+4. Chunk load/generate/send queues must preserve FIFO head order; no starvation fixes may skip a player's queue head.
+5. Entity optimisation must stay read-only unless it can prove vanilla/Paper tick order is unchanged.
+6. Mini-game APIs should expose performance plans so plugin authors can structure large arena work as read-only prewarm + ordered reset/commit.
+
+Next implementation gates:
+
+- Wire `AGCEntitySpatialSnapshotCache` into entity tracker read-only visibility hot paths.
+- Wire `AGCMinigameBurstPlanner` into arena reset/prewarm helpers.
+- Add per-plugin contract weighting to `AGCTickBudgetArbiter` without allowing off-thread Bukkit mutation.
+- Add reproducible simulation tests for 250, 1000 and 3000 synthetic players using packet/chunk/entity/minigame pressure traces.
