+
+### AGC alpha11 aggressive performance mode
+
+AGC alpha11 keeps the aggressive defaults but routes them through a central performance standard:
+
+- central tick budget arbiter across network/chunk/entity/world/player/minigame lanes
+- one-tick latency SLO accounting for low-priority packet batching
+- read-only entity spatial snapshot cache
+- mini-game burst planner for arena start/reset/prewarm waves
+- `/agc hardperf` diagnostics
+
+Aggressive mode is not allowed to get performance by changing visible semantics. It may prepare, snapshot, batch inside a deadline, or wait fairly; it may not drop packets, reorder plugin-visible commits, skip chunk queue heads, or run mutating Bukkit calls off-thread.
